This repository formalizes concepts from the TechNE Hub introductory guide
"Autonomous Operations and Closed Loops" (v1.2.0, 29 October 2026), prepared by
the TechNE Hub 'Measuring and Managing Autonomy (MAMA)' project team
(Project Chair: Emmanuel A. Otchere). The source document's concepts are
attributed throughout docs/ with section-level citations; the realization
model, maturity ladder, vector characteristics, loop taxonomy, latency budgets,
and use-case narratives are harvested from that document. This repository's
model data, schemas, assessment instrument, aggregation rule, engines, site,
and figures are new work (improvements and restatements are marked as such in
model provenance headers and docs/).

Loop specification format alignment: Closed-Loop-Management (CLAM) data model 1.0,
https://github.com/emmanuel-a-otchere/Closed-Loop-Management (Apache-2.0 and MIT
assets as published there; no code vendored).

Related but distinct: the lowercase `mama` autonomy method,
https://github.com/emmanuel-a-otchere/measuring-and-managing-autonomy (MIT).
A loop maturity level is not an autonomy grant level; see docs/naming.md.

The realization model is an informative planning heuristic inherited from the
source document: it must not be used for contractual commitments or
certification purposes (docs/limitations.md).
